From: Wine Fox
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: VirtualProtect gives the old protection of copy-on-write pages as read-write.

Chromium (libcef: Battle.net, other CEF programs) makes a writable section of its own image read-only
after writing it, and checks that VirtualProtect gives PAGE_READWRITE as the old protection: on
Windows a copy-on-write page that was written is a private read-write page. Wine does not track the
written pages and gave PAGE_WRITECOPY: libcef stopped itself (int3, exception 0x80000003), Battle.net's
render process died again and again and Battle.net closed. NtProtectVirtualMemory now gives the old
protection of copy-on-write pages as read-write (execute-read-write); the protection itself and
NtQueryVirtualMemory stay as they are. An unwritten copy-on-write page is given as read-write too:
telling them apart needs tracking of the copied pages.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 84f2a39..06f7120 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -5343,6 +5343,13 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtProtectVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, PVOID *addr_ptr, SIZE_T
         if (get_committed_size( view, base, size, &vprot, VPROT_COMMITTED ) >= size && (vprot & VPROT_COMMITTED))
         {
             old = get_win32_prot( vprot, view->protect );
+            /* Wine does not track which copy-on-write pages were written: on Windows those are
+             * private read-write pages by then, which Chromium (libcef: Battle.net, Steam...)
+             * checks when it seals its writable sections, else it stops itself (int3).
+             * shortcut: an unwritten copy-on-write page is reported as read-write too, real
+             * tracking of the copied pages (as wine-staging does) would tell them apart */
+            if (old & PAGE_WRITECOPY) old = (old & ~PAGE_WRITECOPY) | PAGE_READWRITE;
+            else if (old & PAGE_EXECUTE_WRITECOPY) old = (old & ~PAGE_EXECUTE_WRITECOPY) | PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE;
             status = set_protection( view, base, size, new_prot );
         }
         else status = STATUS_NOT_COMMITTED;
